• the public administration of enterprises is committed to improving services provided, with the user at the center, as a conscious actor, driving a profound transformation, including of production processes, which requires both widely diffused digital competencies (starting from the e-leadership of managers, characterized by a reciprocal contamination of business and digital transformation competencies) and specialist skills;  
• the education system is organized to cover the needs for the development of digital competencies in an organic manner and within a logic of continuity and correlation between the different stages of life and professional training.  
This means that growth connected to the development of digital competencies can only take place within a virtuous cycle, where at the same time all stakeholders, first and foremost, are involved in a comprehensive approach, all public institutions and administrations raising the quality of demands towards other actors and taking on the commitment of change and the "jump" required by digital transformation.

