5.3. | Priorities and intervention priorities

Within the ambit of the 2025 Strategy for Italy, presented on 17 December 2019 by the Minister for Innovation and Digital Transformation of the Country, the initiative "Digital Republic" was included, based on the consideration that digital transformation of the country cannot be separated from the concurrent growth and diffusion of the digital culture. The notable impact of the health emergency makes it even more evident that the use of digital tools is fundamental for social and economic life, as well as for education. In this framework, Digital Republic aims to provide a comprehensive and organic response to the various digital competences, significantly advancing in the following areas:
• On 7 April, the elaboration of the present "National Strategy for Digital Competencies" and the related Operational Plan was launched, which will be consolidated in the coming weeks, starting from existing initiatives;
• On 8 April, the multi-stakeholder alliance established within the framework of Digital Republic entered into the national coalitions for the European initiative on digital competences and jobs (Digital Skills and Jobs Coalition).

4.3.2 Public Sector  
The affirmation and consolidation of competences to support digital transformation require a series of complementary system interventions benefiting both IT specialists and public administration leadership, as well as all personnel involved in the definition and adoption of innovation pathways. The priorities to be addressed are:  
• Promote the hiring of managers prepared to accept and manage the digital transformation of the public sector;

