4.4.2 Public Sector
In relation to the public sector, the impact intended to be achieved, consistent with the expected results of the Strategy, can be summarized as:
• increase in the number of public employees with basic digital competences;
• increase in the number of public employees with specialist ICT skills;
• increase in the number of public digital services targeted at citizens and, above all, to businesses.
The specific indicators are linked to intervention priorities and actions that are intended to be pursued, and, in particular:
• to future public employees selected through pathways that value the role of digital competences applied to the public sector;
• to non-specialist IT public employees who benefit from innovative interventions aimed at supporting the digital transformation, apart from the structural identification of specific needs at organizational, professional, and individual levels;
• to IT specialists who benefit from dedicated selection pathways and highly qualified training interventions.

